PROVISIONAL PATENT APPLICATION

Title: Universal Regulatory Compliance Database Schema and Framework

Inventor: [Your Name]
Filing Date: [Current Date]
Application Type: Provisional Patent Application

TECHNICAL FIELD

This invention relates to database schema architecture and regulatory compliance frameworks that provide universal adaptability across multiple industries and regulatory environments, specifically implementing intelligent field mapping and cross-regulatory compatibility for compliance management systems.

BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION

Regulatory compliance management requires organizations to track, monitor, and report on numerous regulatory requirements across different jurisdictions and industries. Current compliance systems are typically industry-specific and cannot adapt to different regulatory frameworks without extensive customization.

Traditional compliance databases are rigid, requiring separate systems for different regulatory environments. This creates operational inefficiencies, increased costs, and inability to leverage compliance technology across multiple industries or regulatory jurisdictions.

Aviation regulatory compliance, for example, requires tracking FAR Part 142 requirements, while healthcare organizations need HIPAA compliance, and financial services require SOX compliance. No existing system provides universal framework architecture that can adapt to any regulatory environment with simple configuration changes.

SUMMARY OF THE INVENTION

The present invention provides a universal regulatory compliance database schema and framework that can adapt to any industry or regulatory environment through intelligent field mapping, configurable compliance rules, and universal data structures.

The system implements a flexible architecture that maintains consistency across regulatory environments while providing industry-specific customization capabilities. The framework supports aviation (FAR regulations), healthcare (HIPAA, FDA), financial services (SOX, FINRA), manufacturing (ISO standards), and education (accreditation requirements).

Key innovations include:
- Universal compliance data schema adaptable to any regulatory framework
- Intelligent field mapping for cross-regulatory compatibility
- Configurable compliance rule engines for different industries
- Automated regulatory requirement extraction and implementation
- Cross-industry compliance analytics and reporting capabilities

DETAILED DESCRIPTION OF THE INVENTION

Universal Framework Architecture:

