CLAIMS

1. A method for universal regulatory compliance management comprising:
   a) Implementing a universal database schema adaptable to multiple regulatory frameworks
   b) Providing intelligent field mapping for cross-regulatory compatibility
   c) Configuring industry-specific compliance rules and requirements
   d) Generating automated compliance status tracking and reporting
   e) Enabling cross-industry compliance analytics and benchmarking

2. The method of claim 1, wherein the universal database schema includes core compliance entities adaptable to aviation, healthcare, financial services, manufacturing, and education regulatory frameworks.

3. The method of claim 1, wherein intelligent field mapping correlates similar requirements across different regulatory frameworks enabling cross-industry compliance optimization.

4. The method of claim 1, further comprising automated regulatory framework analysis for requirement extraction and intelligent categorization of compliance obligations.

5. The method of claim 1, wherein industry-specific configuration utilizes JSON-based customization for regulatory framework adaptation without database schema modification.

6. A system for universal regulatory compliance management comprising:
   a) Universal database schema supporting multiple regulatory frameworks
   b) Intelligent field mapping module for cross-regulatory compatibility
   c) Configurable compliance rule engine for industry-specific requirements
   d) Automated compliance monitoring and status tracking capabilities
   e) Cross-industry analytics and reporting framework

7. The system of claim 6, wherein the universal database schema implements core compliance entities with industry-specific extension tables for aviation, healthcare, financial services, and manufacturing requirements.

8. The system of claim 6, wherein the intelligent field mapping module maintains correlation tables for similar requirements across different regulatory frameworks enabling compliance optimization.

9. The system of claim 6, further comprising multi-tenant architecture supporting organization-specific compliance framework configuration and cross-organization benchmarking capabilities.

10. The system of claim 6, wherein the compliance rule engine implements dynamic rule generation based on regulatory analysis and automated compliance status calculation.

11. A computer-readable medium containing instructions for implementing the universal regulatory compliance management method of claims 1-5.

12. The method of claim 1, wherein cross-industry compliance analytics identifies overlapping compliance requirements and optimization opportunities across multiple regulatory frameworks.

13. The system of claim 6, further comprising universal API framework providing RESTful endpoints adaptable to any industry with real-time compliance monitoring capabilities.

ABSTRACT

A universal regulatory compliance database schema and framework that adapts to any industry or regulatory environment through intelligent field mapping and configurable compliance rules. The system supports aviation (FAR regulations), healthcare (HIPAA, FDA), financial services (SOX, FINRA), manufacturing (ISO standards), and education compliance through core compliance entities with industry-specific extensions. The invention implements automated regulatory framework analysis, cross-regulatory field correlation, and universal analytics capabilities, expanding total addressable market from $19.6B aviation-specific to $169.6B universal regulatory compliance across all industries while maintaining industry-specific customization and optimization capabilities.

